  "step_1": "The decision reason is based on an aspiration level defined as the mean of all outcomes in the decision problem, ignoring probabilities. The outcomes in the problem are: -4000 (from A), 0 (from A), -3000 (from B), and 0 (from B). The mean of these outcomes is (-4000 + 0 + (-3000) + 0) / 4 = -7000 / 4 = -1750. This is the aspiration level. The reason then evaluates each outcome in both lotteries relative to this level: outcomes above -1750 yield a positive difference, those below yield a negative difference. For Lottery A: -4000 is below -1750 → negative difference; 0 is above -1750 → positive difference. So A has a 80% chance of a positive difference. For Lottery B: -3000 is below -1750 → negative difference; 0 is above -1750 → positive difference. So B has a 75% chance of a positive difference. The reason prefers the lottery with the higher probability of positive differences, which is A (80% > 75%). Thus, the reason can be applied and favors Lottery A.",
